# Everything here is optional. Boxes runs with no .env at all:
#
#   docker compose up -d        ->  http://localhost:3000
#
# Copy this file to .env only to change something. The orchestrator receives
# the whole file and validates it at boot. Unless a note says otherwise, a
# value shown commented out is the default.
#
# No credential goes here. The credentials and the git identity are entered on
# the dashboard's settings page and kept in the data volume, so a change needs
# no restart.

# ---- where the port is published ----
# compose.yaml reads these two to publish the port. BIND_ADDR is the host
# address and HOST_PORT is the host port. The address is loopback by default,
# because the orchestrator has no authentication of its own. Change the address
# only when a different program provides that authentication. A reverse proxy
# on this host reaches 127.0.0.1. A reverse proxy in a container joins the
# boxes_default network and uses orchestrator:3000 instead.
#BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1
#HOST_PORT=3000

# ---- egress ----
# Hosts boxes may reach, comma or whitespace separated. Exact names and
# one-label wildcards: *.example.com matches a.example.com, but not
# a.b.example.com and not example.com. Unset is the default. Then any public
# host is reachable, and private ranges are still denied. The value below is
# an example list, not the default.
#
# A list never cuts a box off from a stored credential's hosts. The OpenAI
# credential also brings auth.openai.com, where Codex logs in and refreshes,
# and chatgpt.com, which a ChatGPT subscription talks to. The proxy never
# sends the credential to those two.
#
# Codex also uses files.openai.com for model attachments and ab.chatgpt.com
# for telemetry. No credential brings these two. When a list omits them, the
# proxy refuses both and the denial counters show it. Codex continues to work.
#
# nix fetches from cache.nixos.org and channels.nixos.org. For a flake named
# github:owner/repo, nix uses api.github.com, github.com and
# codeload.github.com. Without cache.nixos.org and channels.nixos.org, the
# agent cannot install anything with nix.
#EGRESS_ALLOWED_HOSTS=github.com,*.github.com,*.githubusercontent.com,api.anthropic.com,api.openai.com,registry.npmjs.org,cache.nixos.org,channels.nixos.org

# ---- gitlab ----
# The GitLab the settings page token is for, as a bare hostname. Set this only
# for a self-managed instance. The proxy then swaps the token in for that host
# only, and stops intercepting gitlab.com. The instance must have a public
# address, because the proxy refuses private ranges.
#GITLAB_HOST=gitlab.com

# ---- boxes ----
# The image of each box container. The agent cannot install packages with
# apt-get, because the root filesystem is read-only, the agent is not root, and
# the container has no capabilities. The agent installs into /home/agent
# instead. To give every box a package, build an image FROM the published one
# and name it here.
#BOX_IMAGE=ghcr.io/splitbrain/boxes/box:latest
#
# The uid and gid of the box containers, and so the owner of every file in a
# workspace. 1020 keeps clear of 1000, which is the base image's own user and
# often a person on the host. Set these to the uid the orchestrator runs as to
# let the orchestrator drop root.
#BOX_UID=1020
#BOX_GID=1020
# The time between two pulls of the box image, in minutes, so a tag like
# :latest moves here too. The orchestrator also pulls at every boot, so a
# restart gets a new image at once. A running box keeps its image until it is
# next started. 0 turns the refresh off, boot included, for an image built on
# this host. The orchestrator still pulls a missing image once, because it
# cannot create a box without it. Docker only.
#BOX_IMAGE_PULL_MINUTES=60
# True to remove the copies of the box image that a pull replaced. Each copy
# takes disk space, and nothing else removes it. The orchestrator removes only
# replaced copies of the box image. The daemon refuses to remove a copy that a
# container still uses, and the next pull that replaces the image tries again.
# Accepts true, false, 1, 0, yes, no, on or off. Set to false on a host that
# keeps old images to roll back to. Docker only.
#BOX_IMAGE_PRUNE=true
#
# The IPv4 range, in CIDR form, that the orchestrator takes a /24 from for the
# network of each box. The range must be a /24 or larger. A /16 holds 256 box
# networks. Docker only.
#BOX_SUBNET_POOL=10.200.0.0/16
#
# The memory limit of one box container, as a number with an optional suffix
# k, m or g (1024-based). A number without a suffix is bytes. When a box
# reaches the limit, the kernel kills a process in it.
#BOX_MEM_LIMIT=4g
#
# The CPU limit of one box container, in CPUs. A fraction such as 0.5 is valid.
#BOX_CPUS=2
#
# The maximum number of processes in one box container. Docker only.
#BOX_PIDS_LIMIT=512
#
# The minutes without activity after which the orchestrator stops a box. A
# stopped box keeps its files. A box with a running turn, a waiting permission
# request, an attached browser, an open terminal or background work stays on.
#IDLE_STOP_MINUTES=30

# The time in seconds for which a reading of the processes in a box stays
# valid. For each reading, the orchestrator runs ps in the box. It finds work
# such as a command left running in the background. The orchestrator reads at
# this interval while a browser is attached, and at the checks of the idle
# reaper otherwise.
#BACKGROUND_POLL_SECONDS=20

# AGENT_QUIET_SECONDS is the silence in seconds after which the agent of a
# thread counts as stopped. It is a fallback for an adapter that does not mark the
# end of a cycle itself. Codex threads always rely on it.
#
# AGENT_SETTLE_SECONDS is the silence in seconds after which a push
# notification tells that the turn is over. It is longer, because the screen
# can correct itself and a push notification cannot.
#AGENT_QUIET_SECONDS=3
#AGENT_SETTLE_SECONDS=30

# The maximum size of one file that a user attaches to a prompt, in MiB. The
# file service writes attachments to .boxes/attachments/ in the workspace.
#MAX_ATTACHMENT_MB=25

# ---- permissions ----
# PERMISSION_FALLBACK is the action for a permission request that nobody
# answered within PERMISSION_HOLD_MINUTES. hold continues to wait, and deny
# rejects the request.
#PERMISSION_FALLBACK=hold
#PERMISSION_HOLD_MINUTES=120

# ---- notifications ----
# Web Push needs no configuration. The orchestrator generates a VAPID keypair
# at its first use and keeps it in the database. PUSH_SUBJECT is the contact that a push
# service uses when it has a problem with the deployment. It must be a mailto:
# or an https: URL.
#PUSH_SUBJECT=https://github.com/splitbrain/boxes

# ---- logging ----
# Lowest severity written to stderr: debug, info, warn or error.
#
# debug logs every ACP message that the orchestrator forwards between a
# browser and an adapter, in both directions. It is a lot of output on a busy
# deployment.
#LOG_LEVEL=info

# ---- storage ----
# HOST_DATA_DIR is the path of DATA_DIR on the host. The workspace, the home
# and the Nix store of a box are directories under DATA_DIR, and Docker
# bind-mounts them into the box container. The Docker daemon resolves the bind
# source, so the path must be the one the daemon knows DATA_DIR by. Empty is the
# default, and then the orchestrator finds the path at boot from the mounts of
# its own container. With the shipped compose file, that path is
# /var/lib/docker/volumes/boxes_boxes-data/_data.
#
# Set this only where that cannot work, for example for a nested or rootless
# daemon, or for a compose file that mounts a host directory for /data.
# Docker only.
#HOST_DATA_DIR=
